# Windows Active Directory Lab

## Overview

This project demonstrates the deployment and configuration of a Windows Active Directory environment using Windows Server and VirtualBox. The lab simulates a small business network and includes Active Directory Domain Services (AD DS), DNS, Organizational Units (OUs), user and group management, Role-Based Access Control (RBAC), shared folder permissions, and Group Policy Objects (GPOs).

## Technologies Used

* Windows Server
* Active Directory Domain Services (AD DS)
* DNS
* Group Policy Management
* VirtualBox
* NTFS Permissions
* Windows Administration

## Project Objectives

* Deploy a Windows Server Domain Controller
* Create and manage Active Directory users and groups
* Implement Organizational Units (OUs)
* Configure Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)
* Apply Group Policy security settings
* Validate authentication and authorization controls

## Key Accomplishments

* Installed and configured Active Directory Domain Services and DNS.
* Created a new Active Directory forest and domain.
* Built departmental OUs for IT, HR, Finance, Sales, and Workstations.
* Created user accounts and security groups.
* Implemented RBAC using Active Directory security groups.
* Configured shared folders and NTFS permissions.
* Applied password complexity and account lockout policies through GPOs.
* Validated user access and policy enforcement.

## Skills Demonstrated

* Windows Server Administration
* Active Directory Management
* Identity and Access Management (IAM)
* Group Policy Administration
* Access Control
* System Administration
* Enterprise Security



This project provided hands-on experience with enterprise identity management and centralized administration. It strengthened my understanding of Active Directory, DNS, RBAC, and Group Policy implementation in a Windows environment.
